[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2425458177","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/98374#issuecomment-2425458177","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/98374","id":2425458177,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6QkY4B","user":{"login":"BluntBSE","id":31498420,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxNDk4NDIw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/31498420?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/BluntBSE","html_url":"https://github.com/BluntBSE","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BluntBSE/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BluntBSE/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BluntBSE/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BluntBSE/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BluntBSE/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BluntBSE/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BluntBSE/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BluntBSE/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BluntBSE/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-10-21T02:59:59Z","updated_at":"2024-10-21T02:59:59Z","body":"I was able to narrow this down a little further:\r\n`func arrow_to_target_k(origin:CardStub)->void:\r\n\tpass`\r\n\t\r\nThis useless function will cause the crash if the function is set to take an argument of the custom class, CardStub. If the function is defined as accepting no arguments, or an argument of type int, it does not crash.\r\n\r\n","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2425458177/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2425856694","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/98374#issuecomment-2425856694","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/98374","id":2425856694,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6Ql6K2","user":{"login":"pineapplemachine","id":7266412,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNjY0MTI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7266412?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pineapplemachine","html_url":"https://github.com/pineapplemachine","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pineapplemachine/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pineapplemachine/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pineapplemachine/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pineapplemachine/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pineapplemachine/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pineapplemachine/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pineapplemachine/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pineapplemachine/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pineapplemachine/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-10-21T07:35:15Z","updated_at":"2024-10-21T07:35:15Z","body":"Are there parsing errors in `CardStub`? I've encountered similar errors to this that I was able to resolve by fixing errors in the scripts being referenced. It seemed that anything that tried to reference the script with errors sometimes ended up failing to parse, and anything that tried to reference that script and its members, and so on.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2425856694/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2426095919","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/98374#issuecomment-2426095919","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/98374","id":2426095919,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6Qm0kv","user":{"login":"HolonProduction","id":99511741,"node_id":"U_kgDOBe5tvQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/99511741?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction","html_url":"https://github.com/HolonProduction","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-10-21T09:18:48Z","updated_at":"2024-10-21T09:18:48Z","body":"Here is a reduced MRP:\r\n[ultra_mayor_2_reduced.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/17458249/ultra_mayor_2_reduced.zip)\r\n\r\nIt boils down to a bad resolution order when initializing static variables. PilotLibs static init creates LogicPilots which require PilotCardLibs static vars to be initialized, but we try to init PilotLibs static vars first.\r\n\r\n@BluntBSE workaround for you: put a variable `var _dummy: PilotCardLib` into your main menu to ensure that its static variables are intialized before `PilotLib` initializes its static vars.\r\n","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2426095919/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2426210304","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/98374#issuecomment-2426210304","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/98374","id":2426210304,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6QnQgA","user":{"login":"BluntBSE","id":31498420,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxNDk4NDIw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/31498420?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/BluntBSE","html_url":"https://github.com/BluntBSE","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BluntBSE/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BluntBSE/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BluntBSE/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BluntBSE/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BluntBSE/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BluntBSE/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BluntBSE/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BluntBSE/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BluntBSE/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-10-21T10:02:28Z","updated_at":"2024-10-21T10:02:28Z","body":"@HolonProduction How are you able to tell which things are initialized first? I suppose I assumed (perhaps naively) that static vars were all sort of initialized on their own before the program started. \r\n\r\nYour workaround definitely works, I just don't know how you figured that out. This also suggests to me that it's time to change how all these are stored. I was using this static variable as a placeholder for what should probably be a collection of resources.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2426210304/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2426959166","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/98374#issuecomment-2426959166","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/98374","id":2426959166,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6QqHU-","user":{"login":"cranky-corvid","id":109856802,"node_id":"U_kgDOBoxIIg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/109856802?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cranky-corvid","html_url":"https://github.com/cranky-corvid","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cranky-corvid/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cranky-corvid/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cranky-corvid/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cranky-corvid/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cranky-corvid/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cranky-corvid/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cranky-corvid/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cranky-corvid/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cranky-corvid/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-10-21T15:07:19Z","updated_at":"2024-10-21T15:12:05Z","body":"@BluntBSE If you implement `static func _static_init() -> void`, it will be called whenever the static variables of the class are initialized, so you can check exactly when they're getting initialized and from where.\r\n\r\nI don't know all the specifics, but I did previously find that if I load a resource subclass for the 